{"agent":"padap2j","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `set` handler no longer preserves the old error contract, despite the “no behaviour change” claim and the docstring at line 339 (still `tomllib.TOMLDecodeError` when `text` is not TOML, `ValueError` only when the section is not a table). Given `text=\"a = 1\\n\"` (valid TOML), `dotted=\"k\"`, `literal_text=\"!!!\"`, `io.document(f\"v = {literal_text}\")` raises `TomlError`, `io.loads(text)` succeeds, and line 361 raises `ValueError(\"cannot set 'k' to !!!\")` with `from None`. Previously a `TOMLKitError` was re-raised after `tomllib.loads` succeeded. The comment says the `loads` call raises the read-side error callers already handle; that only happens when `loads` itself fails. Any later `TomlError` on valid text (bad literal, or `io.dumps(doc)` failing) is likewise rewritten to a bare `ValueError`, so callers that branch on `TOMLDecodeError` vs “not a table” take the wrong path and the original cause is dropped.","digest":"6054a5d08134bc88","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/infra/tomlcfg.py:359","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/infra/tomlcfg.py:359"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":10956,"diff_sha":"54d4cdef6ef47cede22a9bdee6f3518a702fdd4dd3884ecbcb2b339c2c7d5aea","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/ADP-toml-unify","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":2.1,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"3d7e01c55efaa283","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/ADP-toml-unify.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261110T151831Z-0f9c81d5.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"8443237b03ab","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"75a8d5f562481a2b4ea3a3b219c757e5b7a8cbb9","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/adapte